# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AlphaEngine research portal — data provider keys.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or add in Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables for a deployment. EVERY key is optional: with none set, crypto
# quotes/bars/depth still work through Binance's public endpoints. Each key you
# add lights up more capability — nothing else changes.
#
# GET /api/providers shows, per capability, exactly which of these are live and
# how much of each free-tier quota the running instance has spent.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Financial Modeling Prep — equity quotes (primary), fundamentals (primary),
# daily bars, news. Free: 250 req/day.       https://financialmodelingprep.com
FMP_API_KEY=

# Tiingo — IEX equity quotes, EOD/intraday bars, crypto, news archive.
# Free: 1,000 req/day (personal use).        https://www.tiingo.com
TIINGO_API_KEY=

# Massive (formerly Polygon.io) — equity/crypto aggregates (primary for bars),
# reference data, news. Free: 5 req/min, EOD.       https://massive.com
MASSIVE_API_KEY=
# Point at the legacy host if your key predates the rebrand:
# MASSIVE_BASE_URL=https://api.polygon.io

# Alpha Vantage — quotes, bars, fundamentals, news WITH sentiment scores.
# Free: 25 req/day (ranked last everywhere by arithmetic).
#                              https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# Firecrawl — open-web search + page-to-markdown for filings, exchange
# notices, protocol announcements. Free: 1,000 credits/month.
#                                                  https://www.firecrawl.dev
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# OpenBB — deploy the included stateless `OpenBB_Service/` independently, then
# point this server-only URL at its stable HTTPS origin. The service has no
# portfolio, order, Telegram, or web-UI responsibilities.
OPENBB_API_URL=
# Use the same long random value configured as OPENBB_API_TOKEN on that service.
OPENBB_API_TOKEN=

# Optional connection to the included FastAPI risk gateway. The browser calls a
# same-origin read-only proxy; this URL and token remain server-side. Reliability
# reports the trading path as unobserved when this is absent—it never promotes a
# provider-only snapshot to nominal. In local development an empty URL falls
# back to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
ALPHAENGINE_GATEWAY_URL=
ALPHAENGINE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Optional build-time Ed25519 private key. First pin its public-key SPKI SHA-256
# fingerprint in lib/artifact-trust.mjs. next.config.mjs then uses the private
# key only while building to sign the content-addressed provenance digest; it is
# never compiled into the app. Without both the reviewed trust root and this
# signer, Artifact custody remains fail-closed.
# Generate a PEM with: openssl genpkey -algorithm ED25519
ALPHAENGINE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Systems console — operator actions (POST /api/system/actions)
#
# Read-only telemetry (GET /api/system/health|events|inspect) never needs this.
# The WRITE path does: purging a cache is refilled with live quota, a health
# probe spends a call, and resetting a ledger can let an instance overspend a
# vendor's real allowance. So:
#
#   set    → every action must present `Authorization: Bearer <this value>`
#   unset  → open outside production, and REFUSED (503) in production
#
# Being unset is therefore safe by default on a public deployment, and the
# console shows the reason instead of offering buttons that would 503.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
ALPHAENGINE_OPERATOR_TOKEN=
